  "change_claim": {
    "affected_components": [],
    "architecture_delta": "New xtask modules: metadata, and graph with model, classify, rules, check and report. No new dependency: cargo metadata output is parsed with the serde_json xtask already has.",
    "contract_changes": "none: no product component exists",
    "intent": "Implement the crate-graph checker of plan §5: read `cargo metadata --no-deps --offline`, classify every member totally, evaluate the rha-crates.toml rules, and report findings as JSON, text and markdown with the exit codes §5 fixes. This is the change that makes L0.architecture run, which has blocked the Passed predicate since CHG-000.",
    "non_goals": [
      "The module graph: module_checks reports not_run with reason not_implemented until CHG-007",
      "Transitive mode: --transitive is accepted and prints a notice; [transitive] enabled = true is refused with exit 2, because this version has no transitive evaluator and must not report a requested check as clean (CHG-003.1)",
      "The H4 harness and the fixture generator: `cargo xtask corpus run` is CHG-004",
      "Reading xtask/tests/corpus/manifest.toml from the checker. The manifest is an input to CHG-004's harness, never to the checker; a checker that reads its own test set is not being tested by it",
      "Kennedy's held-out cases (DP-1.1b), which no agent may author or read (§9.14)",
      "Product crates: none exist until CHG-005, so the checker runs over a workspace whose only member is xtask"
    ],
    "performance_impact": "none claimed",
    "source": {
      "path": ".rha/tasks/CHG-003-architecture-crate-level.toml",
      "sha256": "580f7229510ecfd7a8958522b33a5feea4d30cfded6c3b715848623a4d367824"
    },
    "task": "CHG-003",
    "unresolved": [
      "The checker runs over a workspace with one member. Its rules are exercised by unit tests on synthetic graphs and, in CHG-004, by the corpus; nothing in this repository exercises them on real crates until CHG-005.",
      "Authentic still cannot hold (CHG-019, CHG-020), so no record is Eligible even once Passed holds.",
      "An evidence record's agent_context.provenance is copied from the task record, not hashed from the tree (D-002.2.1 on the CHG-002.2 acceptance). A hand-entered digest that goes stale is echoed, not caught, until CHG-019's record lint compares cited digests with the subject tree."
    ]
  },
